    {
      "extraction_class": "Procedure",
      "extraction_text": "3. Factor de forma (Am/V) is the exposed surface area of the element to fire per unit length (Am) divided by the volume of the steel element per unit length (V). If the element is unprotected, Am is its exposed surface. If it is coated, Am is the inner surface of the protection. Only the exposed contour in the analyzed fire sector is considered. For constant section elements, Am/V equals the ratio between the exposed perimeter and the cross-sectional area.",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "e633d289-53b5-442c-8067-17215161313e",
        "parent_section_id": "3de67ea237bc04a3",
        "Procedure": "The shape factor (Am/V) is calculated as the exposed surface area of the element to fire per unit length (Am) divided by the volume of the steel element per unit length (V). Am is the exposed surface if unprotected, or the inner surface of the protection if coated, considering only the exposed contour in the fire sector. For constant section elements, Am/V is the ratio of exposed perimeter to cross-sectional area.",
        "target_reference": [],
